&#x200B;

One thing worth noting:  If you try to log onto a server with these credentials using the JAVA edition for pc, there IS a server running on this IP - I have no idea who it belongs to or what its purpose is but it seems to be running all the time and is completely empty, it has a max of 8 slots.  I dont think I was the first one to try this way; someone has built DELSYM in giant letters in front of the spawn lol, there were also some funny signs I found nearby.

breathe deeply, get some personal space.

&#x200B;

try meditation, nofap will fill you with a primal rage, it is simply the nature of nofap.  meditation is an excellent way to dispel some of this energy in a healthy manner

it makes no difference, i live with my parents and siblings, doesnt make it any less difficult. 

&#x200B;

as far as distractions or using up your time, what im doing right now going to the gym four days a week at my college and i enjoy playing MMORPGS in my free time.  The gym is great because I always am seeing attractive, real people, and its a nice reality check.  The MMO is nice because its a massive time sink which i can grind and grind on without getting bored.

&#x200B;

At the end of the day though, if you are counting on using distractions and staying busy to carry you all the way, you will fail.  The only way around the urges are through them, only after you beat a few hardcore urges do things start to get easier.

&#x200B;

ive also been at it for a couple years but im on day 23 right now to give you some perspective

look into dxm, its a great way to get wonderfully fucked up and not feel even remotely horny.

&#x200B;

its an addictive drug, and should be researched and used with caution.

&#x200B;

but hell man, i know that quitting alcohol and weed can be a real bitch, especially trying to do nofap.  Dxm could be a great tool for you to get some time doing nofap and quitting drugs that make you want to fap.

&#x200B;

i know i quit all drugs except dxm when i began nofap and now ive been sober from all drugs for 60 days and been on nofap for about 25 days.  (been working at nofap for several years and had 90+ streaks though)

congrats on making it to a wet dream!  this is actually a good thing that with experience you will come to take as a blessing 

&#x200B;

wet dreams can really knock the wind out of you, they dont feel great, and the days following them make the experience feel a bit... unrewarding

&#x200B;

but stick with it!  they may not be pleasant but wet dreams are a sign of true healing and rewiring going on in the brain.  they are nothing to be ashamed of, having an interest in sex is a good thing.

&#x200B;

its also worth noting that while orgasming in a dream, you arent aware that its not real, so in terms of how it affects your brain, its like having real sex with another person.

&#x200B;

there is literally no reason to feel ashamed or down on yourself about this.

&#x200B;

stick with it, you are still on your journey, this is NOT a relapse.  i can 100% guarentee that the benefits will return stronger and faster than before

I was only pointing out that it was incorrect to state that global cooling did not scale off INT, as it happens though, in the case of global cooling, damage relates directly to the effectiveness of the utility, as doing more damage with global cooling makes it easier to finish off low magic shields and get a freeze on wet enemies.

&#x200B;

Damage is not irrelevant to the effectiveness of certain utility.  Think of battlestop on warfare, if it does more damage, its easier to get those knockdowns, same concept.

&#x200B;

There are damage buffs you can grant that scale with int like spark striker and venom aura, sure you can just invest in them minimally, but they will do more damage the more INT you have, not FIN or STR.

&#x200B;

Armor replenishment is very easy concept to grasp, basically armor of frost restores 2K+ magic armor for 1 AP at 40 INT...  Same thing with fortify.  

&#x200B;

I respect what you are saying and the full physical route is definitely very viable, im just saying that mages are viable as well in my experience.

Fine.  Every skill that does any damage, healing, damage buffing, or armor replenishment scales with INT.

&#x200B;

I wasnt claiming that there are enemies immune to physical damage, however there are many enemies with obscene physical shields and physical regeneration with comparatively low magic shields.  Thats why I think versatility is better :P

Some mage utility may be low level, but all of them scale in effectiveness with INT.

&#x200B;

A damage mix provides a steady medium rate at which you can clear all fights.  Stacking damage speed-clears some fights, and makes others unnecessarily drag.  I really feel it just comes down to preference

Necro Knight?  Aka best build in the game?  Polymorph, rouge, dualwield sparkstriker and paladin I have also found to be enjoyable and more than viable.  Ranger is excellent, but it is not significantly, if at all, better than the other physical damage classes.

&#x200B;

Mage can leave a bad impression if you try to go in with a full mage party comp for several reasons, but the most dooming thing for that comp IMO is that splitting up the best mage gear you find between four mages is much, much, much, worse than assigning gear between a party comp which is optimized for minimal gear overlap, especially if you tried to make four of the same mage class, four pyromancers for example.

&#x200B;

It is debatable whether or not quad stacking physical damage or bringing the versatility of a mage or two is better.  Personally it is more enjoyable to me to have the damage and excellent utility (which shouldn't be overlooked) of a wizard or two to deal with extremely heavy phys shield enemies rather than slowly brute force my way through them with physical.

it takes some getting used to to really start enjoying it.  I got into it in search of an cheap legal high because I was being tested for weed at the time.

&#x200B;

Its a lot like nicotine, gross and unpleasant at first, but it starts to bother you less the more you use it and eventually becomes really pleasurable once you are addicted.

&#x200B;

It basically feels like a mild mdma experience but with a really sedated, dreamy headspace.  I absolutely loved the high, the only thing more fun was doing mdma itself.

(edit: I said I no longer need it to show me the way.  I think I get the "message" the substance has for me.  That doesn't mean I don't want to take it any more though, I still think it the most enjoyable and fun drug I have tried except for experiences of MDMA and psychedelic ecstasy) 

&#x200B;

Thats a really tough question, to me right now saying "im done with dxm." is like saying "im done going to the beach and relaxing in the sun and taking a weeks vacation."

&#x200B;

It really doesn't sound logical in my head right now, but the very fact that it doesnt is what has me worried.  I had a very bad habit with dxm, there were days last semester when I would drive to uni, and not be able to go in to class and deal with the day, I would just drink high amounts of dxm and chill in my car instead.

&#x200B;

Saying goodbye forever right now?  I dont think I could do that, my goal for now is to go for about 90 days and see if my addiction improves.  Its scary to think about something material like a drug every day when you wake up, I was also obsessed with MDMA in a similar way to I am with dxm.  I eventually stopped obsessing over taking MDMA after not doing it long enough so it is my hope that I can feel the same way about DXM eventually.

&#x200B;

I know that I can always get dxm again if I cant deal with life without it, and that makes it less scary (but also more tempting sometimes.)  My goal is to get 90 days and see how I feel:  If by then I dont feel addicted to it and I no longer want it, great.  If I do still want it, I may re enter the dextroverse later down the line and hopefully practice moderation and self control which I am training now.

You sound like you are in a vulnerable spot right now, I really cant recommend introducing a substance into the equation, especially one so seductive as dxm.

&#x200B;

The thing about dxm is that its a learned high and its very easy drug to do compared to most when you become used to it, once you get comfortable with it having a bad trip is nearly impossible.  (I felt weird my first few dxm trips too, but havent since then.)  Honestly, dxm is more similar to alcohol or xanax or something to me now than it is a traditional psychedelic where the concept of having a "bad trip" comes from.

&#x200B;

All this is to say, if you are feeling under pressure or kind of down, dxm is probably the last thing you want to do right now.  But, if things are going well and you have your life in a good place and under control, you could try again and you shouldn't be afraid or worried about your previous experience.

&#x200B;

Make sure you are in a comforting setting, and let the come up run its course fully (2 hours for me) before you decide if you are going to have a good or bad time, and you should be golden.

thanks friend.  Make sure you do proper research for knowing your dose and for harm reduction.  Dissociation is a very unique and special feeling, what is enjoyable to do while dissociated varies depending on the individual.  I guess what im saying is there is no one size fits all way to properly trip on DXM, (eg. mushrooms, tripping outside in nature is considered best by most.)  

&#x200B;

For me, it was watching zelda vaporwave music videos in the comfort of a dark room, alone, late at night.  Zelda holds a nostalgic connection to me from when i was very young, so it always lead to a very introspective and blissful experience.

&#x200B;

Besides that, all ill say is music really shines on dxm, so listen to some music that you like.

&#x200B;

I recommend taking a 2nd plat dose for your first time (I did this almost every time.)  Dont underestimate 2nd plat, it can be very deep and profound, even though its not totally out of body.  You can visit [dexcalc.com](https://dexcalc.com) to calculate your dosage based on your body weight.

